d clicks \"Send Invite\"\n  2171→- **Expected**: An error message is shown (e.g., \"This email is already a member of the workspace\"). The modal remains open. No duplicate member is created.\n  2172→\n  2173→#### Test: Cancel invite member modal\n  2174→- **Initial state**: User has the Invite Member modal open and has typed \"someone@example.com\" in the email field.\n  2175→- **Action**: User clicks the \"Cancel\" button\n  2176→- **Expected**: The modal closes. No new member is added to the workspace. The members list remains unchanged.\n  2177→\n  2178→#### Test: Close invite modal by clicking backdrop\n  2179→- **Initial state**: User has the Invite Member modal open.\n  2180→- **Action**: User clicks outside the modal (on the backdrop overlay)\n  2181→- **Expected**: The modal closes without sending an invite.\n  2182→\n  2183→#### Test: Invite modal email field can be submitted via Enter key\n  2184→- **Initial state**: User has the Invite Member modal open and has entered \"newuser@example.com\" in the email field.\n  2185→- **Action**: User presses Enter while focused on the email field\n  2186→- **Expected**: The form is submitted, same behavior as clicking \"Send Invite\". The new member is added if the email is valid.\n  2187→\n  2188→#### Test: Invite member modal can be opened multiple times in sequence\n  2189→- **Initial state**: User is on `/settings/members`.\n  2190→- **Action**: User clicks \"Invite Member\", enters \"first@example.com\", clicks \"Send Invite\". Then clicks \"Invite Member\" again, enters \"second@example.com\", clicks \"Send Invite\".\n  2191→- **Expected**: Both members are added to the workspace. The members list shows both new members. The modal opens cleanly with an empty email field the second time (no residual data from the first invite).\n  2192→\n  2193→### MemberActions\n  2194→\n  2195→#### Test: Change member role from Member to Admin\n  2196→- **Initial state**: Workspace has a member \"Bob\" with role \"Member\". Current user is an Admin. User is on `/settings/members`.\n  2197→- **Action**: User clicks the role dropdown for Bob and selects \"Admin\"\n  2198→- **Expected**: Bob's role is updated to \"Admin\". The role badge in Bob's row changes to \"Admin\" with the Admin styling. The change is persisted (reloading the page still shows Admin).\n  2199→\n  2200→#### Test: Change member role from Admin to Member\n  2201→- **Initial state**: Workspace has a member \"Alice\" with role \"Admin\". Current user is an Admin. User is on `/settings/members`.\n  2202→- **Action**: User clicks the role dropdown for Alice and selects \"Member\"\n  2203→- **Expected**: Alice's role is updated to \"Member\". The role badge in Alice's row changes to \"Member\" with the Member styling.\n  2204→\n  2205→#### Test: Role dropdown displays available roles\n  2206→- **Initial state**: User is on `/settings/members`. A member row is visible.\n  2207→- **Action**: User clicks the role dropdown for a member\n  2208→- **Expected**: A dropdown menu appears showing the available roles: \"Admin\" and \"Member\". The currently assigned role is visually indicated (checked, highlighted, or selected).\n  2209→\n  2210→#### Test: Role dropdown can be used multiple times in sequence\n  2211→- **Initial state**: User is on `/settings/members`. A member \"Bob\" has role \"Member\".\n  2212→- **Action**: User changes Bob's role to \"Admin\" via the dropdown. Then user changes Bob's role back to \"Member\" via the dropdown again.\n  2213→- **Expected**: Bob's role first changes to \"Admin\", then back to \"Member\". Both changes are persisted correctly. The dropdown works correctly on the second use.\n  2214→\n  2215→#### Test: Remove member button shows confirmation dialog\n  2216→- **Initial state**: User is on `/settings/members`. Workspace has a member \"Carol\".\n  2217→- **Action**: User clicks the remove/delete button for Carol\n  2218→- **Expected**: A confirmation dialog appears asking the user to confirm the removal (e.g., \"Are you sure you want to remove Carol from the workspace?\"). The dialog has \"Confirm\" (or \"Remove\") and \"Cancel\" buttons. The member is NOT removed yet.\n  2219→\n  2220→#### Test: Confirm member removal deletes the member\n  2221→- **Initial state**: User is on `/settings/members`. The removal confirmation dialog is open for member \"Carol\". Workspace has 3 members.\n  2222→- **Action**: User clicks \"Confirm\" (or \"Remove\") in the confirmation dialog\n  2223→- **Expected**: The dialog closes. Carol is removed from the workspace. The members list now shows 2 members. Carol no longer appears in the list. The removal is persisted.\n  2224→\n  2225→#### Test: Cancel member removal keeps the member\n  2226→- **Initial state**: User is on `/settings/members`. The removal confirmation dialog is open for member \"Carol\".\n  2227→- **Action**: User clicks \"Cancel\" in the confirmation dialog\n  2228→- **Expected**: The dialog closes. Carol remains in the members list. No changes are made.\n  2229→\n  2230→#### Test: Cannot remove yourself from the workspace\n  2231→- **Initial state**: User is on `/settings/members`. The current user's row is visible.\n  2232→- **Expected**: The remove button is either not shown or is disabled for the current user's own row. The user cannot remove themselves from the workspace.\n  2233→\n  2234→#### Test: Cannot change your own role (or last Admin cannot be demoted)\n  2235→- **Initial state**: User is on `/settings/members`. The current user is the only Admin in the workspace.\n  2236→- **Action**: User attempts to change their own role to \"Member\"\n  2237→- **Expected**: Either the role dropdown is disabled for the current user's own row, or an error is shown (e.g., \"Cannot demote the last Admin\"). The workspace must always have at least one Admin.\n  2238→\n  2239→#### Test: Removed member's issues remain assigned but member is gone from selectors\n  2240→- **Initial state**: Workspace has a member 